    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense enters today with a strong outlook, headlined by the two most bankable assets in the lineup: **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (82.65). **Gunnar Henderson** holds the highest efficiency score, benefiting from an elite matchup against Littell and a positive park factor, while his ability to contribute across all five categories\u2014particularly his speed potential\u2014makes him our anchor against a mid-tier arm. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** is positioned to feast on Kochanowicz; the matchup against a weaker starter combined with his spot in the three-hole makes him a high-floor candidate for significant counting stats. Both are must-starts, as their proximity to premium spots in the order provides a high-leverage opportunity for runs and RBI.\n\nThe optimizer leaned into several aggressive platoon edges today, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.62) and **Jackson Merrill** (68.54) both receiving substantial boosts from favorable pitching matchups. **Heliot Ramos** (64.68) also earned a spot due to a massive +10% park factor, effectively creating the separation needed to keep him in the outfield over more speculative plays. Among the bench, **Coby Mayo** (52.34) was the most difficult exclusion. While he benefits from the same favorable matchup as **Gunnar Henderson**, his projected lower spot in the order hampered his cumulative score, and the need to prioritize high-speed options for our scarcity-driven strategy ultimately kept him on the pine.\n\nManagement must remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors. While the model projects **Jackson Merrill**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Andy Pages** into high-order slots, their final efficiency scores could swing if team managers shuffle the batting order. Specifically, **Drake Baldwin** faces the toughest test of the day against Connelly Early\u2019s 2.92 xERA; he remains a start given the position scarcity, but his floor is the 